From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mfmediaengine: IMFMediaEngine(Ex) members that were stubs

Documented behaviour for the members that logged a FIXME and returned E_NOTIMPL
(or a placeholder):

- SetSourceElements: first element whose type is not refused by the extension
  becomes the source (no usable element clears it, with an SRC_NOT_SUPPORTED
  error event); NULL is E_POINTER, MF_E_SHUTDOWN after Shutdown.
- Load runs the resource selection again for the current source (S_OK when
  there is none); IsSeeking follows the seeking state; GetStartTime is 0;
  GetPlayed is an empty range (the whole duration once ended).
- SetAutoPlay/SetLoop without the FIXME (they already round-tripped).
- GetStatistics returns the typed zero for every id (E_INVALIDARG for an
  unknown id, E_POINTER for NULL); UpdateVideoStream validates the rectangles.
- Get/SetBalance round-trip in -1..1 (E_INVALIDARG outside); IsPlaybackRateSupported
  asks the session's rate support; FrameStep is MF_E_INVALIDREQUEST unless a
  video presentation is paused (the session cannot step frames: E_NOTIMPL then).
- Get/Set/ApplyStreamSelections: pending selection per stream, MF_E_NOT_INITIALIZED
  without a presentation, E_INVALIDARG for a bad stream index; IsProtected
  reads MF_SD_PROTECTED of the streams.
- Timeline marker timer (stored, default NaN, cancel resets), stereo 3D
  packing/render mode (validated, round-trip), IsStereo3D FALSE, windowless
  swap chain / mirror / time update timer flags, GetVideoSwapchainHandle
  (MF_E_INVALIDREQUEST unless windowless mode was enabled), IMFGetService
  (MF_E_UNSUPPORTED_SERVICE), class factory LockServer.
All of them return MF_E_SHUTDOWN after Shutdown where that is documented.

